cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use multiprobe in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "multiprobe: Multi-protocol network probing with BGP-correlated divergence analysis"
abstract: >
  multiprobe is a Rust library for multi-protocol network probing combining
  ICMP, UDP, and TCP traceroute with BGP-correlated path analysis.
  It introduces the AS-Boundary Divergence Score (ABDS), a novel metric that
  quantifies routing asymmetry at autonomous system boundaries, and Protocol
  Divergence Localization (PDL) to pinpoint where protocol-specific paths diverge.
  Implements Paris Traceroute for flow-consistent path measurement.
